WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.640
Next, let's talk about your strengths, and I want to make a critical distinction here.

00:08.640 --> 00:11.720
A strength isn't just something you're good at.

00:11.720 --> 00:18.040
You might be excellent at creating complex spreadsheets, but if the process drains every

00:18.040 --> 00:23.320
ounce of energy, that's a learned skill, not a true strength.

00:23.320 --> 00:26.280
A strength is your natural advantage.

00:26.280 --> 00:31.720
It's an activity that you not only do well, but it also energizes you.

00:31.720 --> 00:36.880
It makes you feel authentic and creative and in a state of flow.

00:36.880 --> 00:41.520
Too often, our development plans are about fixing our weaknesses.

00:41.520 --> 00:44.080
An athlete flips that script.

00:44.080 --> 00:47.600
They focus on mastering and deploying their strengths.

00:47.600 --> 00:54.120
They find roles and projects where they can operate from their zone of genius as often

00:54.120 --> 00:55.700
as possible.

00:55.700 --> 01:00.640
This is the fastest path to excellence and impact.

01:00.640 --> 01:04.380
We know you may have heard about focusing on strengths before.

01:04.380 --> 01:10.780
The difference in this experience is that we connect your strengths to your energy.

01:10.780 --> 01:13.940
An athlete doesn't just do what they're good at.

01:13.940 --> 01:19.580
They build their work and life around things that make them feel the most alive.

01:25.700 --> 01:34.900
Your playbook has a drill designed to help you identify the unique talents and highest

01:34.900 --> 01:37.420
value that you bring to the table.

01:37.420 --> 01:42.060
Things that when you do them, you feel most alive and most powerful.

